{"title":"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The perimeter of the isosceles triangle shown is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba318f7385187c693cb1859d9b4b1b587e649d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$53$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> cm.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e824f90df62e600fd7766bc6aec56925cf34c1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  import graph;  real x = 8; // must be &gt; 5.5  pair A = (-5.5, 0); pair B = (5.5, 0); pair C = (0, sqrt(x^2 - (11/2)^2));  draw(A--B--C--cycle);  // points dot(A); dot(B); dot(C);  // vertex labels label(&quot;A&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;B&quot;, B, SE); label(&quot;C&quot;, C, N);  // side labels label(&quot;11&quot;, midpoint(A--B), S); label(&quot;x&quot;, midpoint(A--C), NW); label(&quot;x&quot;, midpoint(B--C), NE); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"155\" />\nThe value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfa69e8c74d5f144844b6ea4cc9c76f343a03e29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\  11\\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 21\\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 20\\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 19\\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As shown from the diagram that shows which sides of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isosceles_triangle\" title=\"Isosceles triangle\">isosceles triangle</a> are equal to each other, we have two sides that are equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> as well as a side that is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The sum of the three side lengths of the triangle will be equal to the triangle's <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perimeter\" title=\"Perimeter\">perimeter</a>.\n</p><p>Thus, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68f14502aa82a26fb1ba7541d951b74492880aa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + x + 11 = 53$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"128\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/c/40c3f270d222f58e54f4c9651cbfcc069211ce11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/2/f22e5b4cca1eccf68dbf907ddaf8e20a117ddc39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Gr